From 65b614e7c405b77252936c4e43853f440dceffd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harsha Nanda <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 16:57:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] perf(platform-web): migrate vitest from jsdom to happy-dom

Switch the platform-web vitest environment to happy-dom to cut per-file
DOM-environment init cost, keeping isolate:true so per-file vi.mock stays
reliable.

One behavioural gap surfaced: happy-dom's Storage is not restorable by
vi.restoreAllMocks() (a vi.spyOn(localStorage,"getItem") mock leaks into
later tests in the same file; jsdom restores it fine). This broke 5
ShellLayout tests that spy getItem to simulate blocked storage and then
rely on real reads afterward. Fixed globally in setup.ts by installing a
standard in-memory Storage (Map-backed, honest get/set/remove/clear/key/
length semantics) whose own configurable methods spy cleanly and restore.
No test assertions were weakened.

All 80 files / 735 tests pass under happy-dom.

Refs kernel issue 09c716d6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
